     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is in the range where liver injury is a real risk. For a 70 kg patient, the toxic threshold is around 150 mg/kg, or about 10.5 g, and this order would reach most of that every day. I don't know of a clinical scenario where that dose is appropriate, and I don't want to put an order into the system that could seriously harm your patient.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours\n\nIf I've misread the order, for example if you meant a different drug or a different unit, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it. If you still need the original dose, I'd suggest talking to a pharmacist first. Any override would have to go through your hospital's own pharmacy and order-verification process, not through me."
      }
     ],
